    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2NrsjZR67sYLkLtKqkMhftf)_\n\n## What\n- **Bug:** `sp-notes-create` failed with `file-name-as-directory: Wrong type argument: stringp, nil`.\n  - Cause (read from the vulpea source): `vulpea-default-notes-directory` is `nil` by default, and `sp-notes-create-file-template` only checked `boundp`.\n  - New `sp-notes-create-base` returns that variable or `sp-notes-filing-root`. The template is relative to it, and `sp-notes-create` binds the variable to it around `vulpea-create`.\n  - `sp-notes-filing-root` itself now uses `bound-and-true-p`.\n- **Load failures:** `sp-move-region-to-heading` no longer requires `denote`. A new note is made with `sp-notes-create` (`sp--create-note-and-get-path`). This also unblocks `sp-tab-inbox` and `sp-tab-psearch`, which require it.\n- **`init.el`:** removed `'sp-notes-filing`. That module was merged into `sp-notes`, so the require failed.\n- Literate docs `sp-notes.org` and `sp-move-region-to-heading.org` updated (bullet lists).\n\n## Next PRs (stacked on this one)\n- `sp-refile` (unblocks `sp-vulpea-ext` and `sp-org-ext`).\n- Leftovers: `sia-denote-link-description-title-case`, `citar-org-node`, comments.\n\n## Testing\n- New ERT test `sp-notes-create-nil-vulpea-default-directory` fails on the old code and passes now; all 17 `sp-notes-test` tests pass in batch Emacs 29.3.\n- `sp-move-region-to-heading` loads with `vulpea` stubbed.\n- /untested/ with the real vulpea, the real vault and the GUI.\n- No CHANGELOG edit.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNi9hnWskPJso94gsTkL)_",
